189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/E (This paper presents constrained language planning, in which language models produce detailed plans for certain objectives while following to constraints. The authors demonstrate that while large language models like InstructGPT are capable of producing reasonable and fluent plans for abstract goals, they frequently fall short of following to specific constraints. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
190 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/E (In order to improve InstructGPT's planning accuracy from 69% to 95%, they suggest an over-generate-then-filter method that creates several candidate scripts and chooses the most constraint-faithful one. In order to train more specialised models, the authors employ this technique to generate CoScript, a dataset containing 55,000 constrained goals and matching scripts. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
191 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/E (Their tests reveal that CoScript-trained models significantly outperform constrained planning, proving that high-quality task-specific data can help smaller models perform on level with, or even better than, much bigger LLMs in certain evaluations. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
