233 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (The authors assess if LLMs can produce plans that accurately adhere to intent, method, and modifier constraints. InstructGPT achieves 97% accuracy on general abstract goals, but when particular limitations are added, its performance drastically declines. Simply adding "Let's think step by step" does not enhance the 175B InstructGPT's overall accuracy on constrained planning, which is only 69%. On the other hand, the suggested over-generate-then-filter approach improves total accuracy by 26 percentage points, reaching 95%. The biggest obstacle is intent limitations, where the suggested approach increases accuracy to 92.86% whereas typical InstructGPT only achieves 42.86%. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (These results show that maintaining the generated steps faithfulness to the given constraint, instead of generating fluent plans, is the main challenge. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
